From 8297f0ecc84bb25aecf714c23dae661cf6cdf626 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rebelancap <7285817+rebelancap@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:34:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] openxr: direct post - VR post pass renders straight into the
 swapchain layer, blitTextures skipped

The OpenXR GL path rendered each eye's post pass into an RGBA8 "L/R Eye"
target and then glBlitFramebuffer'd it into layer 0/1 of the (single,
arraySize 2) swapchain image in endFrame: one extra full-screen copy per
eye per frame. Now the image is acquired and waited for at the left eye's
post pass and the post pass renders into a blaze3d view of the layer
(SwapchainLayerTexture: a GlTexture around the swapchain GL name whose
render passes use the framebuffer OpenGLRawTexture.link already built with
glFramebufferTextureLayer, via FrameBufferCacheVRMixin). endFrame then only
releases and submits.

Off (upstream path) when the swapchain needs the gamma pass, on Vulkan,
while the desktop mirror reads the eye targets (SINGLE/CROPPED/DUAL/MIXED
REALITY or renderAllPasses), and with -Dvivecraft.klepton.directpost=false.
-Dvivecraft.klepton.directpost.selftest=true runs a flat-mode comparison of
both paths on the running GL once (DirectPostSelfTest).
